---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const app = appBySlug('recart')!;
const path = '/apps/recart';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'apps/recart');
const desc = description(site, 'apps/recart');

---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/apps" class="text-sm font-bold text-cyan-300 hover:text-white">← All app reviews</a>
      <p class="badge mt-6">Mobile cart recovery · Rank #5</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{app.name} review for Shopify stores</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-cyan-100">
        Recart is mobile-first cart recovery for promo-heavy Shopify DTC — SMS reminders, Messenger abandoned cart nudges, browse abandonment texts, and discount automation tuned for urgency catalogs. Not a full email platform. When your bottleneck is checkout abandonment on phones and email recovery flatlined, Recart specializes where general ESPs treat SMS as checkbox feature. Pair with Sequenzy or Klaviyo for everything before and after the cart moment.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-cyan-100/90">
        Proposed evaluations cover a hypothetical beauty promotion, a streetwear comparison and a home goods channel comparison. No observed tests or Messenger underperformance are established. Verify current channel availability and account integration before use. Shopify depth: {app.shopifyDepth}.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript review</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Cart recovery guide</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/apps/sequenzy">Pair with Sequenzy</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-12">
    <TldrBox
      title="Verdict: Recart for Shopify"
      picks={[
        { label: 'Focus', tool: 'Cart recovery', reason: 'Mobile SMS and Messenger — not full lifecycle email.' },
        { label: 'Channel mix', tool: 'SMS + Messenger', reason: 'Messenger differentiator vs SMS-only Postscript.' },
        { label: 'Catalog fit', tool: 'Promo DTC', reason: 'Flash sales and urgency products convert on mobile nudges.' },
        { label: 'Pricing', tool: 'Usage-based', reason: 'Monitor message volume during sale weeks.' },
        { label: 'Pair with', tool: 'Sequenzy email', reason: 'Lifecycle before and after cart moment.' },
      ]}
    />

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-white">Why specialization beats generalist SMS checkboxes</h2>
      <p>
        Evaluate mobile recovery economics using actual eligible cart volumes, contribution margin and operating costs. A 40% mobile share or 15% email open rate alone cannot justify a platform; opens are unreliable attention evidence. Verify current capabilities and use randomized eligible comparisons with uncertainty before attributing incremental value.
      </p>
      <p>
        Evaluate whether Messenger and SMS serve the same eligible audience before comparing them. Verify current Recart channel availability, destination rules and Meta requirements. No home goods 2:1 result or beauty parity was observed. Randomize comparable eligible groups where possible and report uncertainty rather than treating channel attribution as causal lift.
      </p>
      <p>
        Recart does not solve list growth, welcome education, post-purchase cross-sell, or winback. Capture still needs Privy or Justuno; lifecycle still needs Sequenzy or Klaviyo. Recart is surgical instrument — excellent at one incision, useless for whole operation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card mb-12">
      <p class="badge">Shopify integration depth</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-white">Checkout events and mobile subscriber growth</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-cyan-100">
        Recart integrates natively with Shopify for cart abandonment, checkout started events, product data in message templates, and subscriber collection via onsite widgets. Revenue reporting attributes recovered orders to SMS and Messenger touches separately — useful for channel mix decisions.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-cyan-100">
        <strong>Standout capabilities:</strong> Abandoned cart SMS sequences, Messenger cart recovery, browse abandonment texts, automated discount escalation with caps, subscriber growth popups, MMS product images, revenue dashboard focused on recovery KPIs.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-cyan-100">
        <strong>Gaps:</strong> No email lifecycle suite. Compliance tooling less enterprise than Postscript. Segmentation depth limited vs Klaviyo. Messenger channel policy dependency creates platform risk. International SMS support varies.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[17px] leading-8 text-cyan-100">
        <strong>Stack coordination:</strong> Assign one sender and queue owner per recovery step. A daily suppression export can become stale; recheck current purpose/channel permission, suppression, purchase and subscription state at dispatch. Reconcile queued cancellations and deduplicate replayed events across senders; verify current integration support rather than assuming sync.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-white">Pricing breakdown with merchant math</h2>
      <p>
        Recart pricing: {app.priceDetail}. Plan tiers plus message usage — model peak sale months.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Scenario A — 420 orders/mo, 1,800 recovery SMS/mo.</strong> Beauty promo brand ~$90–140/mo. Recovered 38 incremental orders/mo at $52 AOV — $1,976 gross vs ~$115 platform cost. ROI positive with margin after COGS.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Scenario B — 1,100 orders/mo, 6,500 SMS plus 2,100 Messenger/mo.</strong> Streetwear ~$220–320/mo peak. Postscript quote similar SMS portion — chose Recart for Messenger incremental lift 8% on holdout test.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Scenario C — 180 orders/mo, insufficient volume.</strong> Recart trial ended — list too small for usage economics. Sequenzy email cart alone sufficient until order volume doubled.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-white">Four workflow tests on Shopify</h2>

      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-white">1. SMS cart recovery — 15% off only on message three</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Proposed scenario:</strong> Hypothetical beauty flash sale with a $64 cart. Evaluate reminder, social-proof and capped 15% discount steps only after validating current sender support and eligibility. Recheck purchase and inventory state at each step; the sequence has not been observed here.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Proposed evaluation:</strong> Test the illustrative $64 beauty cart sequence with randomized eligible alternatives. Check live purchase and inventory state, cancel obsolete steps and deduplicate retries. Measure net contribution after discounts, refunds and message costs with sample sizes and uncertainty. No 13.2% recovery, 41% discount share or margin advantage was observed.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-white">2. Messenger recovery — Instagram traffic cohort</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Proposed scenario:</strong> Hypothetical skincare brand with Instagram-heavy traffic; 70% is an illustrative assumption. Verify current Messenger availability and capture rules before evaluating an eligible mobile-PDP signup and ninety-minute cart reminder.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Proposed evaluation:</strong> Treat the Instagram-heavy skincare audience and ninety-minute reminder as hypothetical. Verify current channel availability and separate channel permission, then compare randomized eligible groups where feasible. No 11.8% versus 9.1% recovery was observed; channel attribution alone does not justify maintaining a channel.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-white">3. Browse abandonment SMS — high-intent collection viewers</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Proposed scenario:</strong> Hypothetical streetwear browser views three products without adding a cart. Evaluate a twenty-four-hour reminder only after verifying browse-event support, live inventory and current purpose/channel permission; no automatic inventory-aware link is established.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Proposed evaluation:</strong> Treat three product views and a twenty-four-hour delay as candidate rules for the streetwear example. Verify browse-event and inventory support, current purpose/channel permission and suppression before dispatch. Cancel after purchase and deduplicate retries. No 6.4% conversion or incremental revenue is established; use randomized eligible comparisons and uncertainty.
      </p>

      <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-black text-white">4. Coordinated recovery with Sequenzy email — holdout test</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Scenario:</strong> Home goods; Sequenzy email cart at 1hr; Recart SMS at 5hr if unopened. <strong>Setup:</strong> 15% holdout SMS-off group.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Proposed evaluation:</strong> The preceding mixed-channel setup is unverified. An unopened email is not current SMS permission or reliable attention evidence. Validate current eligibility and purchase state, assign sender and queue owners, cancel stale steps and deduplicate replayed events. No 5.8% causal lift or failed Messenger test was observed; report randomized eligible comparisons, net costs and uncertainty.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 mb-12">
      <div class="card">
        <p class="badge">Pros</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-cyan-100">
          {app.strengths.map((s) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-300">+</span>{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="badge">Cons</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-cyan-100">
          {app.limits.map((l) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-300">−</span>{l}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2 mb-12">
      <div class="card">
        <p class="badge">Who should buy</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-cyan-100">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-300">→</span>Email cart recovery plateaued on mobile traffic</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-300">→</span>Promo-heavy DTC with urgency catalogs</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-300">→</span>Instagram audience potentially responsive to Messenger</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-300">→</span>400+ orders/mo justifying recovery specialization</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="badge">Who should skip</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-cyan-100">
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-300">→</span>Under 200 orders/mo — email recovery first</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-300">→</span>Need unified Klaviyo or Omnisend stack</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-300">→</span>Enterprise SMS compliance — Postscript</li>
          <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-300">→</span>Full lifecycle in one tool — not Recart's job</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-white">Recart discount discipline and channel testing</h2>
      <p>
        Write discount policy before enabling Recart automations: maximum percentage, which message index, excluded segments (VIP, full-price buyers). Review recovered order margin monthly — gross recovery revenue lies; net margin after discount tells truth.
      </p>
      <p>
        Run 90-day Messenger vs SMS holdout before committing creative resources to Messenger flows. Policy changes at Meta can zero channel overnight — diversify but do not over-invest in fragile channel.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-white">Real merchant stack patterns with Recart</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Beauty promo DTC:</strong> Sequenzy email lifecycle plus Recart SMS cart. Incremental SMS recovery 5.8% over email holdout — Recart bill justified on margin after discount caps enforced.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Instagram skincare Messenger:</strong> Proposed evaluation: verify current channel availability and compare eligible channel groups before assigning creative resources. No observed Messenger/SMS parity is established. Include policy-monitoring labor and matched all-in costs, and distinguish attributed orders from randomized causal contribution.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>180 orders/mo rejected:</strong> List too small for usage economics — Sequenzy email cart sufficient until volume doubled. Revisit Recart when SMS list exceeds 800 opted-in subscribers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card mb-12">
      <p class="badge">Compare alternatives</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-serif text-3xl font-black text-white">Recart vs other Shopify recovery apps</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-lg font-bold">
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript review</a> — SMS-native enterprise alternative</li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Klaviyo vs Postscript</a> — unified vs specialized SMS</li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/smsbump">SMSBump review</a> — Yotpo ecosystem SMS</li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/firepush">Firepush review</a> — web push plus SMS budget option</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container pb-8">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm font-bold">
      <a class="link" href="/apps">All Shopify SMS apps →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Cart recovery →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/for/fashion">Fashion stores →</a>
      <a class="link" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript review →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-12">
      <h2>TCPA, consent, and cost-per-message discipline</h2>
      <p>
        Establish requirements by purpose, channel, destination and sender. Preserve permission evidence and withdrawals; purchase or email signup alone does not authorize promotional SMS. Recheck current suppression, purchase and subscription state at dispatch. Assign queue owners, cancel stale messages and deduplicate retries. Compare matched all-in costs including volumes, destinations, segments, carrier fees, modules, discounts and operating labor; verify current vendor controls.
      </p>
      <p>Model cost per delivered message before scaling broadcasts. A recovered cart that required 25% off plus three texts is often negative contribution margin even when attribution dashboards look green. Pair urgent SMS with Sequenzy email when the message needs education, social proof, or multi-product context — never duplicate the same offer on both channels within twenty-four hours unless the subscriber opted into high-frequency updates.</p>
      <p>Weekly ops: audit STOP/HELP handling, reply inbox backlog, opt-out spikes by flow, and suppression overlap with email cart recovery. Quarterly: re-read popup and checkout consent language against live automations. TCPA litigation and carrier filtering both punish stores that treat SMS like promotional email with shorter copy.</p>
    </div>



</BaseLayout>
